Description: VLC media player 4 for the OnePlus Pad 3 (erhai, SM8750)
 VLC 4 built from the upstream git tree with the erhai VA-API stack: VA-API
 decoding through the Iris driver (H.264, HEVC, VP9, AV1), Wayland/X11 output
 and the Qt interface.  The tree is built with
 --prefix=/usr --libdir=/usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu --enable-vaapi
 --enable-avcodec --disable-kde, so plugins live in
 /usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/vlc/plugins.
 .
 The package is versioned as 4.0.0~git<date>.<commits>+<sha>-0erhai<N> on
 purpose: a later 4.0.0/4.0.x from VideoLAN or Ubuntu sorts higher and upgrades
 over it, while it still outranks Ubuntu's 3.0.23.  It carries no wrapper of
 its own -- oneplus-erhai-av1fix owns that: a dpkg-diverted shim at
 /usr/bin/vlc puts the private libva/libavcodec in front of the player, and its
 file trigger reinstalls the shim after any VLC upgrade.
 .
 This is a monolithic packaging of the VLC tree: no separate vlc-data,
 vlc-bin or plugin packages, and therefore Breaks/Replaces on Ubuntu's vlc 3
 set.  A VLC 4 from the VideoLAN archive supersedes it normally.
